**The Costs of Multi-Account Ecosystems**
The biggest cost comes from the authentication layer alone. You're treating multiple independent accounts as one entity, creating complications around billing, SSO flows, and rate-limiting across all data exchanges. Many platforms like TikTok impose maximum load limits on a single active account (50k requests / second for unverified accounts, or 10k for verified), so recycling agents violates their Rate Limits.

If you want to avoid those limits, consider a reverse proxy pattern: send all requests through one trusted server (like an app running in your home network), and route results locally inside the application to enable lower-latency scraping on the client side.

